Article 12. The People's Court shall accept the following lawsuits brought by citizens, legal persons or other organizations:
(1) Those objecting to administrative penalties such as administrative detention, suspension or revocation of permits and licenses, an order for suspension of production and business, confiscation of illegal gains, confiscation of illegal property, fines, or warnings;
(2) Those objecting to administrative compulsory measures such as restrictions on personal freedom or sealing up, seizure, or freezing of property, or to administrative compulsory enforcement;
(3) Those applying for administrative licenses, where the administrative organ refuses to respond or fails to respond within the statutory time limit, or objecting to other decisions made by the administrative organ concerning administrative licenses;
(4) Those objecting to decisions made by administrative organs concerning the confirmation of ownership or right to use of natural resources such as land, mineral deposits, water bodies, forests, mountains, grasslands, wasteland, tidal flats, and sea areas;
(5) Those objecting to expropriation or requisition decisions and the related compensation decisions;
(6) Those applying to administrative organs to perform statutory duties to protect personal rights, property rights, and other lawful rights and interests, where the administrative organ refuses to perform or fails to respond;
(7) Those considering that administrative organs have infringed upon their rights to autonomous management or rights to rural land contractual management or rural land management rights;
(8) Those considering that administrative organs have abused administrative power to exclude or restrict competition;
(9) Those considering that administrative organs have illegally raised funds, apportioned expenses, or illegally demanded performance of other obligations;
(10) Those considering that administrative organs have not paid pensions, minimum living security benefits, or social insurance benefits in accordance with the law;
(11) Those considering that administrative organs have failed to perform in accordance with the law, performed not in accordance with the agreement, or illegally changed or terminated government concession agreements, land and housing expropriation compensation agreements, or other agreements;
(12) Those considering that administrative organs have infringed upon other personal rights, property rights, or other lawful rights and interests.
In addition to the provisions of the preceding paragraph, the People's Court shall accept other administrative cases that may be brought to court as provided for by laws and regulations.

Article 13. The People's Court shall not accept lawsuits brought by citizens, legal persons or other organizations concerning the following matters:
(1) State acts such as national defense and foreign affairs;
(2) Administrative regulations, rules, or decisions and orders with general binding force formulated and issued by administrative organs;
(3) Decisions of administrative organs on rewards and punishments, appointments and removals of their staff;
(4) Administrative acts that are finally decided by administrative organs as provided for by law.

Article 15. The Intermediate People's Court shall have jurisdiction over the following first-instance administrative cases:
(1) Cases brought against administrative acts performed by departments under the State Council or by local people's governments at or above the county level;
(2) Cases handled by customs;
(3) Major and complex cases within its jurisdiction;
(4) Other cases that shall be under the jurisdiction of the Intermediate People's Court as provided for by law.

Article 31. A party or legal representative may entrust one or two persons as litigation agents.
The following persons may be entrusted as litigation agents:
(1) lawyers and basic-level legal service workers;
(2) close relatives or staff members of the party;
(3) citizens recommended by the community, unit, or relevant social organization to which the party belongs.

Article 33. Evidence shall include:
(1) documentary evidence;
(2) physical evidence;
(3) audio-visual materials;
(4) electronic data;
(5) testimony of witnesses;
(6) statements of the parties;
(7) expert evaluation opinions;
(8) records of inspection and records of the scene.
The above evidence may serve as the basis for determining the facts of a case only after being verified as true by the court.

Article 41: Where the plaintiff or a third party cannot collect the following evidence related to this case on its own, it may apply to the People's Court for obtaining the evidence:
(1) Evidence kept by a state organ which must be obtained by the People's Court;
(2) Evidence involving state secrets, trade secrets or personal privacy;
(3) Other evidence that genuinely cannot be collected on its own due to objective reasons.

Article 49: The institution of an action shall meet the following conditions:
(1) The plaintiff is a citizen, legal person or any other organization that meets the requirements of Article 25 of this Law;
(2) There is a clear defendant;
(3) There is a specific claim and factual basis; and
(4) The case falls within the scope of acceptance of the People's Court and the jurisdiction of the People's Court accepting the case.

Article 96: Where an administrative organ refuses to perform a judgment, ruling or mediation document, the first-instance People's Court may take the following measures:
(1) For a fine that shall be returned or a sum that shall be paid, notify the bank to transfer the amount from the account of the administrative organ;
(2) Where the administrative organ fails to perform within the prescribed time limit, impose a fine of fifty to one hundred yuan per day on the person in charge of the administrative organ, calculated from the date of expiration of the time limit;
(3) Publicly announce the refusal of the administrative organ to perform;
(4) Submit a judicial recommendation to the supervisory organ or the administrative organ at the next higher level. The organ that receives the judicial recommendation shall handle the matter in accordance with the relevant provisions and inform the People's Court of the handling result;
(5) Where the administrative organ refuses to perform the judgment, ruling or mediation document and the social impact is severe, may detain the directly responsible person in charge and other directly responsible persons of the administrative organ; if the circumstances are so serious as to constitute a crime, investigate criminal liability according to law.
